      "message": "In libinit, this make sense because init should have permissions on /system/bin/recovery if it exists. (Assuming that init is the only executable linking libinit)\n\nFor libfs_mgr, you also need to make sure ALL relevant executables that links to libfs_mgr has access to /system/bin/recovery in recovery mode. This includes SELinux permissions and UNIX permissions.\n\n(I am not saying this is incorrect; this is just a reminder for you to check all the binaries linking to libfs_mgr, since you are using this method in a library, not a single binary).",
